        sections: [
          { title: 'Environmental Vocabulary', type: 'rule', content: 'PROBLEMS:\nclimate change / global warming — Earth getting hotter\npollution — contamination (air, water, soil)\ndeforestation — cutting down forests\ndrought — no rain for a long time\nflooding — too much water\nextinction — species dying out completely\nwaste / rubbish — things we throw away\n\nSOLUTIONS:\nrenewable energy — solar, wind, hydroelectric\nrecycling — reusing materials\nsustainability — meeting today\'s needs without harming the future\ncarbon footprint — total CO2 you produce\nconservation — protecting nature\neco-friendly / green — good for the environment\nreduce, reuse, recycle — the three Rs' },
          { title: 'Discussing Environment', type: 'tip', content: 'STATING FACTS:\n"Scientists say that global temperatures have risen by 1.2°C."\n"According to recent reports, sea levels are rising."\n"Deforestation has increased by 20% in the last decade."\n\nGIVING OPINIONS:\n"I believe we need to invest more in renewable energy."\n"In my view, individuals can make a difference by reducing waste."\n"I think governments should ban single-use plastics."\n\nAGREEING/DISAGREEING:\n"I totally agree — we need to act now."\n"I see your point, but I think economic growth is also important."\n"That\'s partly true, but we also need to consider..."' },
          { title: 'Discuss an Issue', type: 'exercise', question: 'Do you think individuals or governments are more responsible for solving climate change? Give reasons.', answer: 'Example: "I think both are responsible, but in different ways. Governments should invest in renewable energy and create laws to reduce pollution — individual action alone isn\'t enough. However, individuals can reduce their carbon footprint by using public transport, eating less meat, and recycling. In my opinion, we need both — government policy creates the system, but individuals make daily choices within it."', answerExplanation: 'Strong B1 opinion answers: state your view → give reasons with "because" → give examples → acknowledge the other side with "however/but." This balanced structure scores well in IELTS and Cambridge exams.' },
        ],
        keyTakeaways: ['Climate change, carbon footprint, renewable energy, sustainability — core terms', 'Reduce, reuse, recycle — the three Rs of environmental action', 'Balance opinions: "Both... however..." shows B1+ complexity'],
